  "notes": [
    "Recordings stay outside the repo, named by hash. They are window captures at one frame a second with the UTC time stamped above each frame (Claude Code terminal: tmux pane text rendered to frames).",
    "Claude desktop evidence without a recording: session 3b23a185 (this spike's own desktop session) held 5 stops and woke twice; session 4efa4b70 (a fresh desktop session in ~/deepbuild-spike80/claude-desk) held 5 stops, showed verdicts, woke on an answer after 32 s idle, and fired FileChanged 3 times during a 65 s call.",
    "Claude desktop: hooks run with PWD set to the session's environment folder, not its working folder; earlier asyncRewake waiters keep running, so one answer woke the session twice (the design assumes a new waiter replaces the old one).",
    "Claude Code 2.1.303: a message typed mid-turn fires UserPromptSubmit at once and is queued; an asyncRewake wake starts its turn with a UserPromptSubmit whose prompt is a task-notification carrying the waiter's stderr; in auto mode a Bash call naming settings.json is denied as [Self-Modification].",
    "Sessions c2d0466d (a terminal session whose environment leaked CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT=claude-desktop) and dry runs are dropped from the logs; payload tool_response fields are dropped.",
    "Oct 19 22:29 UTC, on AC: the fresh desktop session 4efa4b70 held 5 stops, woke on an answer, and fired FileChanged 3 times during a 65.5 s call; no message was typed during the call, and the window showed other sessions, so none of it is on a recording.",
    "22:29–22:33 UTC, this spike's own desktop session on AC: 5 held stops with FAIL verdict lines, then a clean idle wake (wake9b7fff56ee); the window recording showed another session, so it was deleted.",
    "Codex Desktop picks up ~/.codex/hooks.json again on a new turn (after the file was restored, a turn fired no hooks), unlike the CLI, which kept a session's hooks. At 22:43 UTC the reinstalled entries did not fire: the trusted hashes in ~/.codex/config.toml for those entry keys had changed since 20:26 by something outside this spike, and the app skipped them without a review prompt.",
    "Oct 19, 23:12–23:19 UTC: two more desktop calls (60 s and 240 s) with the hooks armed received no typed message, and the throwaway session \"#80 spike: delete me\" (ee1496ed) was not deleted, so the typed and permanent-delete cases stay open.",
    "Oct 19, 23:16 UTC: the Codex CLI listed every spike entry as trusted, yet Codex Desktop 0.160.0 fired none of them on two new turns after ~/.codex/hooks.json was rewritten. The adapter cannot assume the CLI's trust carries to the app; it needs the app's own health reading."
  ]
